            "script": "<p>Part 2 You will hear a talk on the radio about a local festival called the Denford Festival. First you have some time to look at questions 11 to 15.</p>\n<p><span class=\"ts\">(8:15 - 8:30)</span> Now listen carefully and answer questions 11 to 15. I'd like to welcome Sam Goodwin to the programme. He's one of the organisers of this year's Denford Festival.</p>\n<p><span class=\"ts\">(8:31 - 8:53)</span> So, Sam, what can you tell us about what's happening this year? Well, as usual, the festival will take place during the first weekend in August, and there will be things going on all over the town. There are a number of separate areas, each with their own special attraction and atmosphere. Let's start with Bridge Street.</p>\n<p><span class=\"ts\">(8:53 - 9:19)</span> <b data-q=\"11\">Local schoolchildren took part in a competition to paint pictures of the local landscape, and you'll be able to see all their work displayed here.</b> The winning entries have also been made into postcards that you can buy at one of the stalls. <b data-q=\"12\">At Kings Park, we've built a climbing wall, and there'll also be an inflatable bouncy castle for kids</b> to burn off excess energy.</p>\n<p><span class=\"ts\">(9:19 - 9:38)</span> Both are going to be supervised by volunteer teachers at all times, so parents can go off and enjoy other parts of the festival. <b data-q=\"13\">There's a lot happening in Oakvale School. If you're over 18, there's an exciting contest to take part in here.</b></p>\n<p><span class=\"ts\">(9:38 - 10:10)</span> You'll have an hour to prepare your favourite food or dish, and the prizes will be presented by our special guest, the singer Maria Thompson. <b data-q=\"14\">On Green Road, we'll have some top local groups performing and singing throughout the day</b> until 5, including the Denford Choir, who've just come back from a really successful tour of Australia and New Zealand. And finally, I'll mention Sun Lane.</p>\n<p><span class=\"ts\">(10:11 - 10:44)</span> We want you to leave the festival with more than good memories, and a full stomach, so we'd encourage everyone to go to <b data-q=\"15\">Sun Lane, where we'll have a number of experts giving tips and advice on how to successfully grow your own fruit and vegetables.</b> You never know, maybe next year we'll be showing your produce. Before you hear the rest of the talk, you have some time to look at questions 16 to 20.</p>\n<p><span class=\"ts\">(11:19 - 11:29)</span> Now listen and answer questions 16 to 20. Thank you, Sam. That all sounds really interesting.</p>\n<p><span class=\"ts\">(11:29 - 11:48)</span> And you've got some practical information for us. Yes, this year's festival will be bigger than ever, judging by ticket sales so far. <b data-q=\"16\">Tickets can be purchased from our website or at the festival on the day, although those will cost a bit more.</b></p>\n<p><span class=\"ts\">(11:49 - 12:08)</span> The tickets give you free entry to most areas, although you do need to pay extra to get into some of the special events. We're doing something different this year on the final evening of the festival. We usually have a big firework display, but it's proven too expensive this year.</p>\n<p><span class=\"ts\">(12:08 - 12:23)</span> <b data-q=\"17\">So instead, we're holding a dance for everyone who wants to come.</b> That's going to be in the local theatre, where we'll clear away all the chairs to give us plenty of room. It should be great fun.</p>\n<p><span class=\"ts\">(12:25 - 12:47)</span> We're expecting a large number of international visitors, so you'll be hearing a lot of different languages around the festival this year. And we've organised a help desk to advise people on finding accommodation if they need it. <b data-q=\"18\">We'll also be offering day trips to points of interest in the region at very reasonable prices.</b></p>\n<p><span class=\"ts\">(12:48 - 13:04)</span> If you do decide to drive, there are two festival car parks. Car Park A to the north and Car Park B in the east. Car Park B is in the middle of town, so it usually fills up very quickly.</p>\n<p><span class=\"ts\">(13:06 - 13:24)</span> From Car Park A, there is a 15-minute walk along the river to the town centre. <b data-q=\"19\">It takes a little longer to get to the festival, but it's twice the size of B</b>, and it's a nice flat walk. There's one more change I'd like to tell you about.</p>\n<p><span class=\"ts\">(13:24 - 13:47)</span> Last year, we sent out nearly 30,000 free programmes with the tickets, and we're aware of both the cost and the environmental impact of this. We looked into having an app instead, but that was too expensive. <b data-q=\"20\">So, in the end, we decided to put the programme on our website and save that way.</b></p>\n<p><span class=\"ts\">(13:48 - 15:09)</span> You'll still be able to pick up a hard copy at the festival if you want. That is the end of Part 2. You now have 30 seconds to check your answers to Part 2.</p>"
