            "script": "<p>Now turn to Section 2 on page 4. Section 2. You will hear a radio show host interviewing a man called Michael McKay, who is the director of a Canadian theatre. First you have some time to look at questions 11 to 14 on page 4. First you have some time to look at questions 11 to 15.</p>\n<p><span class=\"ts\">(8:59 - 9:14)</span> Now listen carefully and answer questions 11 to 15. Hi, everybody. Thank you very much for agreeing to participate in the next beach clean-up day.</p>\n<p><span class=\"ts\">(9:14 - 9:33)</span> These days are a real benefit for our community. I'm Brenda, the organiser, and I just want to explain a bit about the day to help you prepare and to answer any questions you might have. The beach that's been chosen for the clean-up day is Quinlan Beach.</p>\n<p><span class=\"ts\">(9:34 - 9:59)</span> Because it's easily accessible by public transport, the beach is really popular and well used by locals and tourists alike. The town council does its best to provide bins, but litter is still a problem. <b data-q=\"11\">It's important to deal with this, as it's a threat to the groups of seals that swim around there</b> and regularly rest on the flat rocks.</p>\n<p><span class=\"ts\">(10:00 - 10:16)</span> When you observe them in their natural habitat, you really sense why you're picking up this litter. You'll be working in groups of three to four people at the beach. Some of you have signed up as groups already, which is great.</p>\n<p><span class=\"ts\">(10:17 - 10:27)</span> The rest of you will be organised into groups on the day. <b data-q=\"12\">There are different roles in the group. It'll be up to you to choose who does what in the group.</b></p>\n<p><span class=\"ts\">(10:28 - 10:41)</span> After lunch, we'll form new groups, which will give you a chance to get to know new people. You may be wondering what kind of equipment you'll need. You may have seen tools to pick up litter with.</p>\n<p><span class=\"ts\">(10:41 - 10:55)</span> They're like poles with a sharp end. <b data-q=\"13\">If you want to use one of those, you'll have to bring your own.</b> After the safety briefing, we'll give you each a whistle to blow in case you need to get our attention.</p>\n<p><span class=\"ts\">(10:56 - 11:16)</span> The town council is providing special collection bags for us to use, which are fully biodegradable. There are a few things to keep in mind regarding clothing for the day. <b data-q=\"14\">Definitely go for something comfortable and wear shoes or boots that will keep your feet dry.</b></p>\n<p><span class=\"ts\">(11:17 - 11:35)</span> We're all going to be given yellow caps so we can identify each other. The town council is supplying vinyl gloves, but they're quite large, so your own may be more comfortable. Sunscreen is up to you, but highly recommended.</p>\n<p><span class=\"ts\">(11:37 - 12:00)</span> Each group that goes out picking up litter will be given a survey to fill in as you go along. The town council can get an estimate of the quantity and the different kinds of litter we gather up by examining the bags we collect. <b data-q=\"15\">However, they are very keen to know more about where you find the rubbish, which may help them in future.</b></p>\n<p><span class=\"ts\">(12:00 - 12:58)</span> So that's what you're asked to indicate on the survey. OK, now please look at the map showing Quinlan Beach. When you arrive, you can park in the car park, which is at the bottom of the map.</p>\n<p><span class=\"ts\">(12:58 - 13:19)</span> The first aid station is close to the shore and will be staffed all day in case anyone needs it. <b data-q=\"16\">You can find it by taking the footpath that goes north from the car park towards the beach. The path branches out, but carry on straight and there it is.</b></p>\n<p><span class=\"ts\">(13:20 - 13:39)</span> To get to the equipment pickup, <b data-q=\"17\">walk along the road that leads from the car park, around the bend and past the bus stop. There's a small building before you get to the golf club and that's where the equipment is kept.</b> You'll want to know where the toilets are.</p>\n<p><span class=\"ts\">(13:40 - 13:59)</span> <b data-q=\"18\">They're adjacent to the car park, on the opposite side from where the wooded area is.</b> You can see the beach is sort of divided into two stretches by rocky point. <b data-q=\"19\">The meeting point for the beach cleanup is on the beach that's closest to the cafe.</b></p>\n<p><span class=\"ts\">(14:00 - 14:12)</span> Later in the day, you'll move to the West Beach. We'll be meeting for lunch at 1pm. Some food is available in the cafe or you can bring your own.</p>\n<p><span class=\"ts\">(14:13 - 14:55)</span> <b data-q=\"20\">We'll meet in the area immediately outside the entrance to the Grand Pier where there are picnic tables.</b> You get a good view from there. So now, if there are any questions... That is the end of Part 2. You now have 30 seconds to check your answers to Part 2.</p>"
